1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Hi. In this video, we'll use Burp Suite to test for blind XXE vulnerabilities.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,600
Blind XXE injection vulnerabilities occur when an application is vulnerable to XXE injection,

3
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:22,000
but doesn't return the values of any defined external entities within its responses.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
This means that direct retrieval of server-side files isn't possible.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:34,000
You can use Burp to inject an XXE payload that may trigger an out-of-band network interaction with the Burp collaborator server.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Burp monitors the collaborator server to identify whether an out-of-band interaction occurs.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
This indicates that the XXE attack was successful.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:52,000
If you'd like to follow along with this demo, you can use the lab Blind XXE with Out-of-band Interaction from our Web Security Academy.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Once the lab has launched, we need to identify a request that contains XML that we want to investigate.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:07,000
For this lab, we're going to check the stock for an item and then go to the Proxy HTTP History tab to find the request.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Right-click the request and choose Send to Repeater.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Insert an XXE payload into the XML string.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The payload should define an XML entity and contain a collaborator subdomain as a value.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:35,000
We can add the collaborator subdomain by right-clicking and selecting Insert collaborator payload.

15
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Click Send.

16
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Now go to the collaborator tab.

17
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,000
If the collaborator has been polled and interactions have been detected, the tab will flash.

18
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,000
When you go to the tab, you can click Poll Now to poll for the latest interactions.

19
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
The results will be listed in the table.

20
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:06,000
If an entry appears in the table for the collaborator subdomain you used, this indicates that the XXE attack successfully triggered an interaction.

21
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:11,000
There may be a delay before any interaction with the collaborator server occurs.

22
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
So make sure you continue to check the tab to identify any delayed interactions.

23
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:23,000
You can test additional XML data values by replacing a different data value in the XML with your defined XML entity.

